@startuml compact_admitted_execution
title Compact Runtime - Admitted Execution Only
' Source baseline: pi-mono-java@bfc7ad88 modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/RuntimeSessionEngineRegistry.java:register,withOperationLock,complete.
' Source baseline: pi-mono-java@bfc7ad88 modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/session/ManagedAgentSession.java:compact,close.
' This PR: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/compaction/RuntimeCompactionCoordinator.java:CompactionRun.
' This PR: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/compaction/RuntimeCompactionExecution.java:result.
' Design baseline: pi-mono-java-design@0a113ce8 Built-in README section 7.
' Observed pi behavior: pi@4af9d21d packages/coding-agent/src/core/agent-session.ts:compact persists then rebuilds messages.
' Java divergence: idle-only admission, global capacity, database projection and cancellation-isolated completion.
' Design reason: Compact must never enter the POST Events control-queue continuation path.
' Target-only: row-locked admission and empty-history observation are implemented in the next slice.
skinparam shadowing false
participant "Future admission service\n(not wired in this PR)" as Caller
participant "Compaction coordinator\nper-run state under shared operation lock" as Run
participant "Active Holder\nManaged Session" as Holder
participant "Shared Projector\npersistence-only output" as Projector
database "Session Repository" as Repository
participant "Shared Registry\ncapacity + timeout scheduler" as Registry
participant "Independent result\nminimal CompletionStage" as Result
note over Caller,Holder
  Precondition: accepted running state, registered Holder,
  shared capacity acquired, internal Usage run ID assigned.
  Execution rejects controls from construction time.
end note
Caller -> Run : start(holder, execution)
Run -> Holder : subscribe compaction events
Run -> Registry : schedule default 30-minute timeout
Run -> Holder : compact(no custom instructions)
Run --> Caller : cancellation-isolated result handle
alt completed normally
  Holder -> Run : completed domain event
  Run -> Projector : project under operation lock
  Projector -> Repository : append Compaction Entry + Usage
  Repository --> Projector : actual Entry sequence
  Holder -> Run : compaction Future completed
else failure or timeout
  Registry -> Run : timeout (or execution failure)
  note right of Run
    Do not wait for an uncooperative Future.
    Do not persist generic command lifecycle.
  end note
end
group one-time terminal cleanup under operation lock
  Run -> Run : mark finished; clear callback target
  Run -> Holder : unsubscribe
  Run -> Registry : complete only matching execution
  Registry -> Holder : close (abort compaction; clear queues)
  Registry -> Registry : release capacity even if close throws
  Run -> Repository : finishExecution (running -> idle)
  note right of Run
    Attempt every cleanup step; preserve failures.
    Failed idle persistence means failed result.
    No Steer, FollowUp or queued continuation.
  end note
  Run -> Result : complete with actual sequence or failure
end
Holder -> Run : late event or completion
Run -> Run : ignore detached or finished callback
@enduml
